Development Workflow Instructions

Running the Application

Always remember to run the backend first, then open a new terminal for each of the three.

Backend:
cd backend
npm run dev

Mobile:
cd mobile
flutter run

Web:
cd web
npm run dev


Branching

1. First, go to the dev branch, then fetch and pull the latest changes using github application.

2. If you are creating a new branch, the base branch must be dev.

3. Branch names should use an appropriate prefix depending on the purpose:

feature/ — new feature
fix/ — bug fix
refactor/ — code restructuring
docs/ — documentation
style/ — styling or formatting
chore/ — maintenance/configuration
test/ — tests
perf/ — performance improvement
hotfix/ — urgent fix

Examples:
feature/doctor-registration
fix/appointment-status
refactor/auth-service
docs/update-documentation


Changes to the Code

1. Before making any changes, always prompt the AI:

"Read all of the .md files inside the docs folder to know what to do, especially AGENTS.md."

2. After finishing your assigned task, prompt the AI:

"Read and perform GitHub_Desktop_Commit_Grouping_Instructions.md."

3. The AI will provide the files that need to be CHECKED and UNCHECKED for each commit. Follow those instructions in GitHub Desktop, then use the provided commit message to commit and push your changes.